# RQ1. Do flagged and unflagged instances have different resolution rates after accounting for difficulty? 
• Independent variable: Exposure-screening status (flagged/unflagged). 
• Dependent variable: Resolution rate (%). 
• Analysis: Compare resolution rates between flagged and unflagged instances within difficulty 
groups, combining the two highest-duration bands. 

# RQ2. Does removing flagged instances produce a larger resolution-rate decrease than removing the same 
number of unflagged instances matched by difficulty? 
• Independent variable: Removal condition (flagged/matched unflagged). 
• Dependent variable: Excess resolution-rate decrease (percentage points). 
• Analysis: Compare the observed resolution-rate decrease after flagged-instance removal with the 
mean decrease from repeated difficulty-matched removals of the same number of unflagged 
instances. Report excess decrease, relative decrease, and uncertainty. 
• Hypothesis: Flagged-instance removal produces a larger decrease. 

# RQ3. Does excess resolution-rate decrease differ across difficulty groups? 
• Independent variable: Difficulty group. 
• Dependent variable: Excess resolution-rate decrease (percentage points). 
• Analysis: Compare group-specific estimates and uncertainty, interpreting small groups cautiously. 
